  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Above seasonal temperatures and dry conditions \nwill prevail throughout the week. A cold front will bring \ncooler temperatures this weekend. \n\nNow that the front has moved through and the remnants of\nIsaias are now out of our hair, drier and warmer conditions will\nmove into the area. High pressure will build over the central US\nthrough the early half of the week and slowly build eastward by\nthe end of the week. This will lead to dry conditions through\nthe work week and the only concern will be for near record highs\ngiven the strength of the upper ridge. Temperatures by the end\nof the week will be in the upper 80s to maybe even 90 degrees\nacross some interior areas. This will certainly flirt with some\nrecord highs as we go through the week. By the weekend, our next\nsystem will swing through as the upper trough breaks down and a\ncold front moves through the area bringing significantly cooler\nconditions to the area.",
